@JobLens.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5183

# POST /ingest and POST /run share one exclusive, cross-process pipeline-run
# lock (%LOCALAPPDATA%\JobLens\run.lock) - only one of them can be mutating
# pgvector at a time. If the lock is already held (by the other endpoint, or
# a concurrent call to the same one), the request returns immediately with:
#   409 Conflict
#   {"error":"Another JobLens pipeline run is already in progress."}
# instead of doing any feed/parse/embed/score work.

# Ingest only: fetch -> parse -> category filter -> dedupe -> embed -> upsert.
# It never scores, notifies, or drafts - newly stored postings are left unscored
# so the next POST /run picks them up off the backlog and scores them exactly
# once. Response:
#   {"fetched":3,"parsed":3,"filteredOut":1,"alreadyStored":0,"newlyStored":2}
POST {{JobLens.Api_HostAddress}}/ingest
Accept: application/json

###

POST {{JobLens.Api_HostAddress}}/run
Accept: application/json

###
